D string; the record’s own ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when its context has no session","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The event’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event\/name","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as it is","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"properties"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The event’s stored properties, by name, then the members listed below"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timestamp"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the event was tracked: ISO 8601 in UTC, with milliseconds ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"2026-11-23T14:03:27.512Z"},{"type":"text","text":")"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"uuid","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID string; a redelivered record keeps it"}]}]]],"header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The session is the only identifier sent, and every event is anonymous: ","type":"text"},{"code":"properties","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" holds","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"$process_person_profile: false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so PostHog makes no person profile, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"$geoip_disable: true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so PostHog doesn’t add a location from the request’s IP address. A record with no session (one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tracked by a tracker without ","type":"text"},{"code":"Enricher.sessions()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or one a store recovered after a relaunch,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which keeps no context) is its own anonymous person, linked to nothing: PostHog rejects a whole","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"batch when one of its events has no ","type":"text"},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". PostHog counts a person per ","type":"text"},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so its unique users are sessions. The session is also sent as ","type":"text"},{"code":"$session_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which PostHog’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sessions and web analytics group events by (","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the UUIDv7 they require); a record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with no session has none. The record’s vendor identifier and trace context, and any other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"context value, aren’t sent.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read from the event’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"BinaryCodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" form, which ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" derives, through the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"types its schema in ","type":"text"},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lists: a ","type":"text"},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a string; a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Bool","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" a boolean; an integer, a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Float","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" a number; a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Date","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" an ISO 8601 string, as ","type":"text"},{"code":"timestamp","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is; a ","type":"text"},{"code":"UUID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"uppercase UUID string; an array an array; and an optional’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A ","type":"text"},{"code":"Refined","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is its value. A ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"property is left out, and an element of an array is ","type":"text"},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A property whose name starts with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"$","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which only a hand-written ","type":"text"},{"code":"BinaryCodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformance can write, or is ","type":"text"},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"left out and logged at notice level, as PostHog reads those names as settings (","type":"text"},{"code":"$set","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"$process_person_profile","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") or the identity.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"properties"},{"text":" also holds these members, for each of the keys the record’s context has a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Member"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Key","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Holds","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_namespace"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_version"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_build"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ApplicationKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The bundle identifier, version and build, each left out when ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"$device_model","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$device_type","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"DeviceKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The model, and "},{"code":"Mobile","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Tablet","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Desktop","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"TV","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"Vision","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for the form factor; no "},{"code":"$device_type","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for a watch"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"$locale","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocaleKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The locale’s BCP 47 identifier, such as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"en-US"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$network_wifi"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$network_cellular"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"NetworkKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Whether the connection is Wi-Fi, and whether it is cellular","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os_name"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os_version"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OperatingSystemKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The operating system’s name and version"}]}]]],"header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the body, and the batch’s other records are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sent: one whose event and version ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"text":" doesn’t describe, one whose event name starts with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(a name PostHog keeps for its own events), one whose event isn’t ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BinaryCodable"},{"text":", or one that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"holds a value JSON can’t (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogEncodingError","isActive":true},{"text":"). Each is logged at error level;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/batch(of:)","isActive":true},{"text":" returns them as ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogSkippedRecord","isActive":true},{"text":"s. When every record of a batch is left","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out, ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/encode(_:)","isActive":true},{"text":" throws, so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" sends nothing for it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"PostHog answers a batch it takes with 200, so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" retries one that gets no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"response, a 5xx, 408 or 429, and drops one it rejects. A record sent again keeps its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"uuid"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The bytes are the same for the same records on every run and platform: no whitespace, object","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"members in the order of their names’ UTF-8 bytes. PostHog takes a body of up to 20 MB, so keep","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"batches far smaller (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch()"},{"text":" sends 20 records at most).","type":"text"}]}]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatch"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Encoding-batches","title":"Encoding batches"}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://PostHogEncoding/documentation/PostHogEncoding/PostHogSkippedRecord":{"title":"PostHogSkippedRecord","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PostHogSkippedRecord"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PostHogSkippedRecord"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogSkippedRecord","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/posthogencoding\/posthogskippedrecord","abstract":[{"text":"A record ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder","type":"reference"},{"text":" left out of a batch’s body, and why.","type":"text"}]},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/BatchEncoder":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"What turns a batch of records into the body of the request ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" sends.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/batchencoder","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BatchEncoder","kin